# Social-Media Share Cards for Character Pages — Plan

**Status:** Plan document only. Proof-of-concept built (Ross Kinley). Full batch deferred until after the sandbox commit. Pick up from here.

---

## Goal

Each of the 91 character pages in `NETWORK_PEOPLE_SANDBOX/people/*.html` needs a 1200×630 social-share image (Open Graph + Twitter Card) so that when the URL is pasted into Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Discord, Slack, iMessage, etc., it previews as an intentional branded card rather than a random page screenshot or nothing at all.

Currently:
- 91 pages in `/people/`
- **0** of them have `og:image` tags
- The big three (Dominic, Ethel, Isla) link to external sites (`dominicryker.com`, `ethelryker.com`, `islaband.com`) — those have their own cards and are NOT in scope here

---

## Design spec

**Dimensions:** 1200 × 630 px, JPEG q=92 (Facebook/Twitter optimal)

**Palette (VeX dark, matches the network UI):**
- Background near-black warm: `rgb(8, 6, 4)`
- Vellum cream text: `rgb(237, 226, 200)`
- Secondary cream dim: `rgb(180, 168, 144)`
- Brass accent: `rgb(212, 169, 76)`
- Brass deep (footer): `rgb(160, 122, 48)`
- Oxblood reserved for future variants: `rgb(94, 26, 26)`

**Layout:**
```
┌─┬──────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ │                                          │
│B│   ⬭   DISPLAY NAME (large serif)         │
│R│  (av) @handle (mono, brass)              │
│A│   ⬭                                      │
│S│       bio / tagline (italic serif)       │
│S│                                          │
│ │              VEX · SILENCEISTHETRAUMA.COM│
└─┴──────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- Brass left-edge stripe (6px wide)
- Avatar circular-masked at ~440px, brass rim, positioned at `x=84, y=center`
- Display name: Georgia Bold 78px, vellum
- `@handle`: Consolas 32px, brass
- Bio (from `profiles.json`): Georgia Italic 34px, cream-dim, max 3 lines wrapped
- Footer: Arial Bold 18px tracked caps, brass-deep, bottom-right
- Subtle vignette + 6% paper-grain noise overlay across the canvas

**Verified tick:** small brass `✓` next to the display name if `profile.verified === true`.

---

## Per-character data — pull from `profiles.json`

For each profile entry, the template uses:
- `id` — output filename: `assets/images/social_share/{id}.jpg`
- `handle` — `@text`
- `display_name` — large title
- `avatar` — path resolved relative to `vex_network/`
- `bio` — tagline (italic cream-dim)
- `verified` — controls the tick
- `links_to` — **only generate if this points into `../people/`. Skip external URLs.**

---

## In scope / out of scope

**In scope:** the ~88 character pages whose `links_to` points to a local `../people/*.html` page.

**Out of scope (external sites with their own cards):**
- `@dominic_ryker` → `https://www.dominicryker.com`
- `@ethel_ryker` → `https://ethelryker.com`
- `@isla_band` → `https://islaband.com`
- Any other handle whose `links_to` starts with `http`

**Memorial / silent profiles** (Gran, Pop, Isla's Mother): still in scope — they have pages, and the share card stays useful as biographical signage even though they don't post. Cross-check against `feedback_dont_touch_character_websites.md` and `project_dead_characters.md` before doing anything beyond *adding meta tags* (don't touch their actual page content).

