The script (originally in `files.html` at the body level) prepends the
current page's folder path to any nav href that doesn't start with `/`,
`#`, or `http://`. That's correct for root-level pages where the nav uses
bare relative hrefs (`files.html` -> `/files.html`), but it's WRONG for
sub-folder pages where the nav already uses depth-aware relative hrefs
(`../files.html` -> turns into `/short_stories/../files.html`, which the
server treats as a different path -> 404).

Converted archives and stories have correct depth-aware hrefs and need
no normalization. This patch wraps the script body in an early-return
so it doesn't run on those pages, keeping the file otherwise identical
to the 7-page shell.
